    {
      "id": "i6XSpkga6nnXXRGgLGKFZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2394.1579793572473,
      "y": -85.09578530901854,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "HZD8P7g6n33eje2UUghKT",
        "SmF3s_zitTIFqUBOcIIzx",
        "c5Ba4U2NNLa48xxD_UrI4",
        "uWyv-nJ7GyW7Wtsi3aI4F",
        "LRgzwmMPVlKCumhpjKAjW",
        "kteS11Y8BNUHDfqlwO-b4",
        "22Cgnlk3RRqNTlNk2EVHO",
        "IkYIZLzPZIF7OR7eg3vAj"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 398520692,
      "version": 8253,
      "versionNonce": 2060870900,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791530743587,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "People need to know things.\n\nInfobesity—also known as information overload or infoxication—is the state of feeling overwhelmed,\nstressed, or unable to make decisions because you are consuming or receiving too much data.\n\nInformation retrieval or IR is the name of the field encompassing the retrieval of all manner of media\nbased on user information needs. The resulting IR system is often called a search engine.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis figure abstracts over the two classes of IR systems, which are based on the two classes of\nvectors that are used to represent queries and documents: sparse vectors and dense vectors. \nIn sparse retrieval, we represent documents and queries with count vectors.\nIn dense retrieval, we represent documents and queries with embeddings, computed from language models.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "People need to know things.\n\nInfobesity—also known as information overload or infoxication—is the state of feeling overwhelmed, stressed, or unable to make decisions because you are consuming or receiving too much data.\n\nInformation retrieval or IR is the name of the field encompassing the retrieval of all manner of media based on user information needs. The resulting IR system is often called a search engine.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis figure abstracts over the two classes of IR systems, which are based on the two classes of vectors that are used to represent queries and documents: sparse vectors and dense vectors. \nIn sparse retrieval, we represent documents and queries with count vectors.\nIn dense retrieval, we represent documents and queries with embeddings, computed from language models.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791468099807,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
