      "updated": 1791530743587,
      "created": 1791530538752,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Inverted Index",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Inverted Index",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "d8CKg8beqlGI-TA0gZULW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2365.8977546464757,
      "y": 3316.0656418358067,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "sG4hd6sgWRG2NJDrLdKjU",
        "-_2BvHRzNiIAa3mqgz3Qm",
        "eZOW8HrzxGd5oikuEcHCJ",
        "exngvVt9qJM0z3FoAvB97",
        "JI3sX-LaOK8_kHh0IU9b3",
        "MmNhm-k3bA-SdeDtdSm4q",
        "H6XmkrSyTAk671MWl96ll",
        "uOeKS_31XQEC_QpK4xovr",
        "hn6fZRCTPlyWEbRioptpV"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1722198004,
      "version": 8355,
      "versionNonce": 911051636,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791530743587,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In order to compute scores, we need to efficiently find documents that contain words in the query. The\ndata structure for this task is the inverted index, which we use for making this search efficient\n\nAn inverted index, given a query term, gives a list of documents that contain the postings term. It\nconsists of two parts, a dictionary and the postings. The dictionary is a list of terms (designed to be\nefficiently accessed), each pointing to a postings list for the term. A postings list is the list of\ndocument IDs associated with each term, which can also contain information like the term frequency or\neven the exact positions of terms in the document. The dictionary can also store the document\nfrequency for each term.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGiven a list of terms in query, we can very efficiently get lists of all candidate documents, together with\nthe information necessary to compute the tf-idf scores we need.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In order to compute scores, we need to efficiently find documents that contain words in the query. The data structure for this task is the inverted index, which we use for making this search efficient\n\nAn inverted index, given a query term, gives a list of documents that contain the postings term. It consists of two parts, a dictionary and the postings. The dictionary is a list of terms (designed to be efficiently accessed), each pointing to a postings list for the term. A postings list is the list of document IDs associated with each term, which can also contain information like the term frequency or even the exact positions of terms in the document. The dictionary can also store the document frequency for each term.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGiven a list of terms in query, we can very efficiently get lists of all candidate documents, together with the information necessary to compute the tf-idf scores we need.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791530552760,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
