      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BEIR",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BEIR",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.15,
      "created": 1791468069863,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DWeimUKafnbwiLc8rEEbT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3236.974922259651,
      "y": 12489.383338605026,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "X_GifWUpTULUXkLOlmoLA",
        "NnN2MIw5KJ_WPTb5RRMzk",
        "AJ1iJcXTA1DdTFtVLwYl7",
        "QqDljHAfhsu6tjvuGVq94",
        "j6p7BALQpZZmjSNtHcmfs",
        "pXuKcAkHnWXwz_Abmp2V1",
        "mdVMqTeUuBGSPK_r2kuOE",
        "Vx7pjJEjLrN1C7ou2FDQu",
        "yCefckdtgwU5-2LZ-nl5m",
        "6nnEJSv8wki6u3kZidZ4d"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2E",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1227030220,
      "version": 8779,
      "versionNonce": 1910333388,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791573754757,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "BEIR (Benchmarking IR) is one of the most influential benchmarks in modern Information Retrieval\n\nIt was designed to evaluate the zero-shot generalization of retrieval models: how well a model performs\non datasets, domains and retrieval tasks it has not been specifically trained on.\n\nBEIR brings together 18 diverse datasets covering 9 retrieval tasks, including question answering, fact\nverification, scientific document retrieval and argument retrieval.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBesides covering different tasks, BEIR also varies along several dimensions:\n- Domains: Wikipedia, biomedical research, finance, scientific literature, news and social media.\n- Corpus sizes: Approximately 3,600 to 15 million documents.\n- Query lengths: From short keyword queries to longer natural-language questions or claims.\n- Document lengths: From short social media posts to full scientific articles.\n- Relevance criteria: Answering a question, supporting a claim, expressing a similar meaning or identifying\na relevant entity.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "BEIR (Benchmarking IR) is one of the most influential benchmarks in modern Information Retrieval\n\nIt was designed to evaluate the zero-shot generalization of retrieval models: how well a model performs on datasets, domains and retrieval tasks it has not been specifically trained on.\n\nBEIR brings together 18 diverse datasets covering 9 retrieval tasks, including question answering, fact verification, scientific document retrieval and argument retrieval.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBesides covering different tasks, BEIR also varies along several dimensions:\n- Domains: Wikipedia, biomedical research, finance, scientific literature, news and social media.\n- Corpus sizes: Approximately 3,600 to 15 million documents.\n- Query lengths: From short keyword queries to longer natural-language questions or claims.\n- Document lengths: From short social media posts to full scientific articles.\n- Relevance criteria: Answering a question, supporting a claim, expressing a similar meaning or identifying a relevant entity.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1791572083563,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
